05 [P1] Matrix axes and row count are listed before completion is claimed.\n- [ ] CHK-FIX-006 [P1] Hostile env/global-state variant executed when tests or code read process-wide state.\n- [ ] CHK-FIX-007 [P1] Evidence is pinned to a fix SHA or explicit diff range, not a moving branch-relative range.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:fix-completeness -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:security -->\n## Security\n<!-- FILL: Write one check per security surface. Write `N/A` with a reason when none applies. GOOD: CHK-030 [P0] The script reads no credential. WEAK: Security is fine. -->\n\n- [ ] CHK-030 [P0] No hardcoded secrets\n- [ ] CHK-031 [P0] Input validation implemented\n- [ ] CHK-032 [P1] Auth/authz working correctly\n<!-- /ANCHOR:security -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:docs -->\n## Documentation\n<!-- FILL: Write one check per document that must agree. GOOD: CHK-040 [P1] `spec.md` and `tasks.md` name the same flag. WEAK: Docs are updated. -->\n\n- [ ] CHK-040 [P1] Spec/plan/tasks synchronized\n- [ ] CHK-041 [P1] Code comments adequate\n- [ ] CHK-042 [P2] README updated (if applicable)\n<!-- /ANCHOR:docs -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:file-org -->\n## File Organization\n<!-- FILL: Write one check per file location rule. GOOD: CHK-050 [P1] Test copies live under `scratch/test/`. WEAK: Files are organized. -->\n\n- [ ] CHK-050 [P1] Temp files in scratch/ only\n- [ ] CHK-051 [P1] scratch/ cleaned before completion\n<!-- /ANCHOR:file-org -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:summary -->\n## Verification Summary\n<!-- FILL: Count the boxes by priority and write the three totals. GOOD: P0 12, P1 13, P2 1. WEAK: Most items done. -->\n\n| Category | Total | Verified |\n|----------|-------|----------|\n| P0 Items | [X] | [ ]/[X] |\n| P1 Items | [Y] | [ ]/[Y] |\n| P2 Items | [Z] | [ ]/[Z] |\n\n**Verification Date**: 2026-10-25\n<!-- /ANCHOR:summary -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:arch-verify -->\n## L3+: Architecture Verification\n<!-- FILL: L3+ means Level 3 and above, so this section stays at Level 3. Write one check per ADR, or delete the section when the packet records no ADR. GOOD: CHK-100 [P0] ADR-001 is followed by T002. WEAK: Architecture is verified. -->\n\n- [ ] CHK-100 [P0] Architecture decisions documented in decision-record.md\n- [ ] CHK-101 [P1] All ADRs have status (Proposed/Accepted)\n- [ ] CHK-102 [P1] Alternatives documented with rejection rationale\n- [ ] CHK-103 [P2] Migration path documented (if applicable)\n<!-- /ANCHOR:arch-verify -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:perf-verify -->\n## L3+: Performance Verification\n<!-- FILL: L3+ means Level 3 and above, so this section stays at Level 3. Write one check per performance claim, or delete the section when the packet makes none. GOOD: CHK-110 [P1] The flag adds under 5 ms. WEAK: Performance is verified. -->\n\n- [ ] CHK-110 [P1] Response time targets met (NFR-P01)\n- [ ] CHK-111 [P1] Throughput targets met (NFR-P02)\n- [ ] CHK-112 [P2] Load testing completed\n- [ ] CHK-113 [P2] Performance benchmarks documented\n<!-- /ANCHOR:perf-verify -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:deploy-ready -->\n## L3+: Deployment Readiness\n<!-- FILL: L3+ means Level 3 and above, so this section stays at Level 3. Write one check per deployment step, or delete the section when the packet ships no service. GOOD: CHK-120 [P0] The rollback command was run in a copy. WEAK: Ready to deploy. -->\n\n- [ ] CHK-120 [P0] Rollback procedure documented and tested\n- [ ] CHK-121 [P0] Feature flag configured (if applicable)\n- [ ] CHK-122 [P1] Monitoring/alerting configured\n- [ ] CHK-123 [P1] Runbook created\n- [ ] CHK-124 [P2] Deployment runbook reviewed\n<!-- /ANCHOR:deploy-ready -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:compliance-verify -->\n## L3+: Compliance Verification\n<!-- FILL: L3+ means Level 3 and above, so this section stays at Level 3. Write one check per compliance surface, or delete the section when none applies. GOOD: CHK-130 [P1] No license changed. WEAK: Compliance is verified. -->\n\n- [ ] CHK-130 [P1] Security review completed\n- [ ] CHK-131 [P1] Dependency licenses compatible\n- [ ] CHK-132 [P2] OWASP Top 10 checklist completed\n- [ ] CHK-133 [P2] Data handling compliant with requirements\n<!-- /ANCHOR:compliance-verify -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:docs-verify -->\n## L3+: Documentation Verification\n<!-- FILL: L3+ means Level 3 and above, so this section stays at Level 3. Write one check per document pair that must agree, or delete the section when the packet holds no paired documents. GOOD: CHK-140 [P1] `plan.md` and `tasks.md` agree on the three phases. WEAK: Docs are verified. -->\n\n- [ ] CHK-140 [P1] All spec documents synchronized\n- [ ] CHK-141 [P1] API documentation complete (if applicable)\n- [ ] CHK-142 [P2] User-facing documentation updated\n- [ ] CHK-143 [P2] Knowledge transfer documented\n<!-- /ANCHOR:docs-verify -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:sign-off -->\n## L3+: Sign-Off\n<!-- FILL: L3+ means Level 3 and above, so this section stays at Level 3. Name the real approver for each role. Delete a row when the role does not exist. Write `N/A` or delete the section when no sign-off applies. GOOD: Conductor, runs every task. Operator, merges the commit. WEAK: Signed off. -->\n\n| Approver | Role | Status | Date |\n|----------|------|--------|------|\n| [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Name] | Technical Lead | [ ] Approved | |\n| [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Name] | Product Owner | [ ] Approved | |\n| [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Name] | QA Lead | [ ] Approved | |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:sign-off -->\n\n\n","newText":"---\ntitle: \"Tasks: Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh\"\ndescription: \"Task Format: T### [P?] Description (file path). Verify: <command> prints <expected output>\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"recommend level quiet flag tasks\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: tasks-core | v2.3 -->\n# Tasks: Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh\n\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 3 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:notation -->\n## Task Notation\n\n| Prefix | Meaning |\n|--------|---------|\n| `[ ]` | Pending |\n| `[x]` | Completed |\n| `[P]` | Parallelizable |\n| `[B]` | Blocked |\n\n**Task Format**: `T### [P?] Description (file path). Verify: <command> prints <expected output>`\n\n**Paths**: `S` is `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh`; `T` is `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/test-phase-validation.js`.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:notation -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n## Phase 1: Setup\n\n- [ ] T001 Read the output functions and the dispatch in the script (`S`). Verify: `rg -n 'output_text|output_json' S` prints two definitions and one dispatch site.\n- [ ] T002 Record the default report length before any edit (`S`). Verify: `bash S --loc 500 --files 15 --auth --api --db --architectural | wc -l` prints 17.\n- [ ] T003 [P] Confirm `--quiet` is not accepted today (`S`). Verify: `bash S --quiet --loc 10 --files 1` exits 1 with `ERROR: Unknown option: --quiet`.\n- [ ] T004 [P] Record the test baseline (`T`). Verify: `node T | tail -1` prints `Result: passed=51 failed=0`.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n## Phase 2: Implementation\n\n- [ ] T005 Add `QUIET=false` to the globals block (`S`). Verify: `rg -n 'QUIET=false' S` prints one line.\n- [ ] T006 Add the `--quiet` case to the argument parser (`S`). Verify: `bash S --quiet --loc 10 --files 1` exits 0.\n- [ ] T007 Add `output_quiet()` beside the other renderers (`S`). Verify: `rg -n 'output_quiet' S` prints the definition.\n- [ ] T008 Dispatch to `output_quiet()` before the JSON branch (`S`). Verify: `bash S --quiet --loc 500 --files 15 --auth --api --db --architectural | wc -l` prints 1.\n- [ ] T009 Document the flag in the header OPTIONS block and in `show_help()` (`S`). Verify: `bash S --help | rg -c -- '--quiet'` prints 1.\n- [ ] T010 [P] Add the one-line contract case to the harness (`T`). Verify: `node T | tail -1` prints `Result: passed=52 failed=0`.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n## Phase 3: Verification\n\n- [ ] T011 Verify the exact quiet line (`S`). Verify: `bash S --quiet --loc 500 --files 15 --auth --api --db --architectural` prints `Recommended Level: 3 (Full)`.\n- [ ] T012 Verify the default report is unchanged (`S`). Verify: `bash S --loc 500 --files 15 --auth --api --db --architectural | wc -l` prints 17.\n- [ ] T013 Verify the JSON document still parses (`S`). Verify: `bash S --json --loc 500 --files 15 --auth --api --db --architectural | node -e 'let s=\"\";process.stdin.on(\"data\",d=>s+=d).on(\"end\",()=>console.log(JSON.parse(s).recommended_level))'` prints 3.\n- [ ] T014 Verify the error path stays silent on stdout (`S`). Verify: `bash S --quiet --loc abc >/dev/null; echo $?` prints 1.\n- [ ] T015 Verify the flag composes with phase suppression (`S`). Verify: `bash S --quiet --no-recommend-phases --loc 500 --files 15 --auth --api --db --architectural | wc -l` prints 1.\n- [ ] T016 Verify the script still parses (`S`). Verify: `bash -n S` exits 0 with no output.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:completion -->\n## Completion Criteria\n\n- [ ] All tasks marked `[x]`\n- [ ] No `[B]` blocked tasks remaining\n- [ ] Manual verification passed\n- [ ] The four `--quiet` x `--json` combinations are recorded in the verification summary\n<!-- /ANCHOR:completion -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n## Cross-References\n\n- **Specification**: See `spec.md`\n- **Plan**: See `plan.md`\n- **Acceptance criteria**: See `acceptance-criteria.md`\n<!-- /ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n\n---\n\n## Verification Checklist\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:protocol -->\n## Verification Protocol\n\n| Priority | Handling | Completion Impact |\n|----------|----------|-------------------|\n| **[P0]** | HARD BLOCKER | Cannot claim done until complete |\n| **[P1]** | Required | Must complete OR get user approval |\n| **[P2]** | Optional | Can defer with documented reason |\n\n### Pre-Task Checklist\n\nBefore starting any task, confirm: the script path resolves, `git rev-parse --abbrev-ref HEAD` names the expected branch, the baseline in T002 is recorded, and the task's `Verify:` command has been run once against the unmodified tree so the \"before\" output is known.\n\n### Execution Rules\n\n| Rule | Meaning |\n|------|---------|\n| TASK-SEQ | Run tasks in numeric order; T003, T004, and T010 may run in parallel with their neighbours |\n| TASK-SCOPE | Touch only the file named in parentheses on the task line |\n| TASK-EVIDENCE | Mark a task `[x]` only after its `Verify:` command printed the expected output |\n| TASK-REGRESSION | After T008, rerun T002 before running any other verification |\n\n### Status Reporting Format\n\nReport each task as `T### PASS|FAIL - <observed output>`. A failure names the command, its exit code, and the first differing line. Do not summarise a failure as \"does not work\".\n\n### Blocked Task Protocol\n\nMark a task `[B]` when its `Verify:` command fails twice for the same reason, when the script's structure no longer matches the line numbers named in the plan, or when a change would be needed outside the two files in scope. Record the failing command and its output on the task line, then stop and report.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:protocol -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:pre-impl -->\n## Pre-Implementation\n\n- [ ] CHK-001 [P0] Requirements documented in spec.md\n- [ ] CHK-002 [P0] Technical approach defined in plan.md\n- [ ] CHK-003 [P1] Dependencies identified and available\n<!-- /ANCHOR:pre-impl -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:code-quality -->\n## Code Quality\n\n- [ ] CHK-010 [P0] `bash -n` exits 0 on the edited script\n- [ ] CHK-011 [P0] No new shellcheck finding at warning severity or above (skip when shellcheck is absent)\n- [ ] CHK-012 [P1] Every existing exit 1 path still exits 1 with the same stderr text\n- [ ] CHK-013 [P1] The new code sits in the existing section layout: globals, renderers, dispatch\n<!-- /ANCHOR:code-quality -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:testing -->\n## Testing Checklist\n\n- [ ] CHK-020 [P0] AC-002 holds: `--quiet` prints one line matching the label regex\n- [ ] CHK-021 [P0] AC-003 holds: the default report still prints 17 lines\n- [ ] CHK-022 [P0] AC-004 holds: `--quiet --json` prints the text line and no JSON\n- [ ] CHK-023 [P1] AC-006 holds: `--quiet --loc abc` exits 1 with an empty stdout\n- [ ] CHK-024 [P1] AC-007 holds: `--help` names `--quiet`\n- [ ] CHK-025 [P1] The Node phase suite reports `failed=0`\n<!-- /ANCHOR:testing -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:fix-completeness -->\n## Fix Completeness\n\n- [ ] CHK-FIX-001 [P1] Same-class producer inventory: `rg -n 'Recommended Level' S` names the one producer line\n- [ ] CHK-FIX-002 [P1] Consumer inventory completed for the label and the flag: two test files, the skill README, and two asset documents\n- [ ] CHK-FIX-003 [P1] Matrix rows executed: `--quiet` x `--json` in all four combinations, and `--quiet` x valid/invalid input in both outcomes\n<!-- /ANCHOR:fix-completeness -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:security -->\n## Security\n\n- [ ] CHK-030 [P0] No hardcoded secret or token is added to the script\n- [ ] CHK-031 [P0] Input validation for `--loc`, `--files`, and `--phase-threshold` is unchanged\n- [ ] CHK-032 [P1] The flag reads no environment variable, file, or credential\n<!-- /ANCHOR:security -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:docs -->\n## Documentation\n\n- [ ] CHK-040 [P1] Spec/plan/tasks name the same flag and the same one-line format\n- [ ] CHK-041 [P1] The script header OPTIONS block and `--help` both list `--quiet`\n- [ ] CHK-042 [P2] The skill README needs no edit: it lists the script but documents no options\n<!-- /ANCHOR:docs -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:file-org -->\n## File Organization\n\n- [ ] CHK-050 [P1] Any scratch file lives under this packet's `scratch/`\n- [ ] CHK-051 [P1] `scratch/` is cleaned before completion\n<!-- /ANCHOR:file-org -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:summary -->\n## Verification Summary\n\n| Category | Total | Verified |\n|----------|-------|----------|\n| P0 Items | 10 | 0/10 |\n| P1 Items | 18 | 0/18 |\n| P2 Items | 4 | 0/4 |\n\n**Verification Date**: 2026-10-25\n<!-- /ANCHOR:summary -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:arch-verify -->\n## L3+: Architecture Verification\n\n- [ ] CHK-100 [P0] ADR-001 is followed: the dispatch checks `QUIET` before `JSON_OUTPUT`\n- [ ] CHK-101 [P1] ADR-002 is followed: `output_quiet()` prints the same label `output_text()` prints\n- [ ] CHK-102 [P1] Both ADRs record their rejected alternatives\n- [ ] CHK-103 [P2] Migration path: not applicable, because the flag is opt-in per invocation\n<!-- /ANCHOR:arch-verify -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:perf-verify -->\n## L3+: Performance Verification\n\n- [ ] CHK-110 [P1] NFR-P01 holds: `--quiet` performs the same scoring pass and prints one line instead of 17\n- [ ] CHK-111 [P2] Throughput target: N/A, a single-shot CLI with no server\n<!-- /ANCHOR:perf-verify -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:docs-verify -->\n## L3+: Documentation Verification\n\n- [ ] CHK-140 [P1] All four packet documents name `--quiet` and the `Recommended Level: <N> (<Name>)` line\n- [ ] CHK-141 [P2] User-facing documentation is `--help` alone; no other surface describes the options\n<!-- /ANCHOR:docs-verify -->\n","_meta":{"cognition.ai/linesAdded":74,"cognition.ai/linesRemoved":108}}],"rawInput":{"file_path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/217-weak-model-spec-authoring/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/tasks.md"},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"write"}}
